okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: `F:\\omini-router 에서는 아예 리쥼 세션이 하나도 안 나오는 문제..` - after the --continue resolution fix no omini-router session could be resumed at all; find why and fix it."
symptom: "`ciel-runtime muse --continue` in F:\\omini-router did not restore the 15 MB session; Muse ended up in the session picker, which listed nothing (`Resume a previous session ... 0 / 0 ...`)."
diagnosis:
  stale_lock_refusal: "`muse resume 01a0b860-89c9-7110-a9a6-2c8b63fba897` answered `that session is already open in another window — pick another session (held by pid 36399 on SAMA)` although pid 36399 died in the 2026-09-19 WSL restart. Moving only that session's `.session.lock` aside made the same resume open the session (`Initializing runtime` -> `Restoring conversation`) and append 24 records (`session.resumed`, `session.opened.observed`, `runtime.session.task_source_committed` x6, `session.end` x2). Muse's staleness check does not clear a lock whose pid is gone (at least on this host)."
  locks_everywhere: "All 25 session directories in the store carried a `.session.lock`; 23 named dead pids. Muse's picker excludes sessions it considers open (`Current session is already open and was excluded.`), which is why it showed 0 rows in every workspace tested (omini-router, aap.ezonebot, ciel-runtime, home)."
  history_dead_reference: "The omini TUI history ends with `01a0bb7e-4f99-7bc1-aaf4-7d9eddaacdfa` (recorded 16:06) whose session directory does not exist anywhere in the store, so the previous `--continue` resolver could pick a dead id."
  index_row_pruned: "The session's index row was stuck as `missing_metadata` because Muse's projector fails on its log (`tool-call batch with 1 call(s) was not committed` - the session was killed mid-tool-call). Advancing the file mtime made the next reconcile delete the row instead of repairing it. After one successful resume (lock cleared) Muse wrote recovery records, `muse trace inspect` then completed (`Result: completed`, no projection error), and the reconcile wrote a valid row: workspace_root=/mnt/f/omini-router, prompt_count=36, name=brown-procyon, latest_segment_terminated=1, indexed 17:56."
  picker_still_empty: "After clearing stale locks, the runtime-registry leftovers (`runtime/muse/sessions/<id>.json`, `ms-*.sock`, `.lease`) of dead sessions, the bare `muse resume` picker still renders only its header with `0 / 0` and opens no store files; its worker never starts. That layer is Muse-side (1.3.0-R3401.1, build 3c572bc734) and is not fixed here."
fix:
  - "muse_runtime_context: before any launch whose argv resumes (a `resume` token), sweep `$HOME/.local/share/muse/sessions/*/*/*/*/.session.lock` and remove locks whose pid no longer exists and whose host is this machine; locks held by a live pid stay. The launch log records `muse_stale_lock_sweep removed=N`."
  - "`_resolve_continue` now takes the newest TUI-history ids for the workspace and picks the first whose session directory exists (`session_exists_script`, one bounded WSL probe), and it resolves a bare `resume` (Muse's picker, which lists nothing here) to that session instead of opening the picker. Explicit refs (`resume <name>`, `resume <id>`) are left untouched."
verification:
  unit: "tests/test_muse_runtime.py: history ordering/dedupe, existence-probe script shape, picker launch resolves to the existing session while skipping the missing newest one, explicit refs untouched (and no history read), fallback to the newest id when nothing exists, sweep runs for resume launches only. Unit group 1583 tests OK (skipped=45); ruff clean."
  live_direct: "With the lock moved aside, a pty `muse resume 01a0b860... --yolo` opened the session (`Restoring conversation`); the log grew 15318317 -> 15332185 bytes (13428 -> 13452 lines)."
  live_launcher_cycle1: "`ciel-runtime muse --continue` from F:\\omini-router on snapshot 1b68bdf: instance log `muse_continue_resolved session=01a0b860-89c9-7110-a9a6-2c8b63fba897 workspace=/mnt/f/omini-router`, `muse_stale_lock_sweep removed=0`, muse argv `/home/djlov/.local/bin/muse-bin-1.3.0-R3401.1 resume --yolo --model muse-spark-1.3 --reasoning-effort high 01a0b860-89c9-7110-a9a6-2c8b63fba897`, and the TUI restored the conversation (footer `muse-spark-1.3 · high · /mnt/f/omini-router · YOLO`, transcript lines present, no picker)."
  live_launcher_cycle2: "That session was killed (leaving a dead-pid lock, like any crashed session); the same launch then logged `muse_stale_lock_sweep removed=1` and `resume ... 01a0b860-...` opened the session again - no `already open` refusal. Cleanup left only the user's own Muse process (pid 748, aap.ezonebot) running and the omini router (9489) stopped."
  artifacts: "/tmp/860-session-backup.jsonl (sha256 de5bf71cdf2acce8a62feed83021b100ba701217ebe0e921957b7245fa5d568f) was byte-identical to the live log after the mtime-only experiment; /tmp/muse-registry-backup-20260919/ holds the registry files removed while probing; no session directory was deleted."
also_observed:
  - "Muse's session picker (bare `muse resume`, and the same picker the TUI opens) lists nothing on this host even with locks, registry entries and sockets cleared; resume by id/name/--continue no longer depend on it, so the launcher resolves a bare `resume` itself instead of opening the empty picker."
  - "Resume recovery printed `resume quarantined cron:01a0b860... (store_unavailable): the session cron store could not be opened: cron store backend error: database is locked` - scheduled tasks are disabled for that session; cause not investigated."
  - "A `ciel-runtime muse` launched from inside a ciel-runtime session inherits `CIEL_RUNTIME_LAUNCH_CWD`/`CIEL_RUNTIME_STATE_DIR`, so the launcher resolved the parent session's workspace (port 9611) instead of the shell cwd; the confirmation runs cleared those variables."
cleanup: "Verification added resume/end records to 01a0b860 (13428 -> 13490 lines); its index row is valid again. The user's own Muse sessions were never touched."
not_done:
  - "Muse-side: the picker list stays empty; the projector refuses logs that end in an uncommitted tool-call batch and the reconcile deletes such rows until a successful resume rewrites recovery records."
